+# Sources consulted
+
+- **vSAN Cluster Deployment Options** — Broadcom Support, consulted 2026-08-14, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/326549/vsan-cluster-deployment-options.html — used to confirm that a stretched vSAN cluster distributes hosts across two data sites, survives the loss of a site, uses a witness at a third site, and requires no more than 5 ms between data sites.
+- **vSAN Health Test 'Site latency health' status changed from 'green' to 'yellow'** — Broadcom Support, consulted 2026-08-14, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/412056/vsan-health-test-site-latency-health-sta.html — used to confirm the 5 ms data-site and 200 ms witness latency limits for stretched vSAN.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — Broadcom Support, consulted 2026-08-14, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — used for the mandatory VCF Operations-first sequence, VCF Management Services, centralized license server, management-service IP requirement, and 5.2.x-to-9.1 LCM path.
+- **Correlating VMware Cloud Foundation version with the versions of its constituent products** — Broadcom Support, consulted 2026-08-14, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/314608/correlating-vmware-cloud-foundation-vers.html — used to confirm the pinned VCF 5.2.2 constituent versions for SDDC Manager, vCenter Server, ESXi, vSAN Witness, and NSX.
+- **Update path from VMware Cloud Foundation or VMware vSphere Foundation V8 to V9** — Broadcom Support, consulted 2026-08-14, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/437250/update-path-from-vmware-cloud-foundation.html — used to confirm that a V9-eligible subscription entitlement and VCF Operations are prerequisites for V9 licensing.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation Installer API Reference Guide 9.1.0.0** — VMware by Broadcom, consulted 2026-08-14, https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/blob/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer/vcf-installer-openapi.json — used for the installer `SddcSpec` fields and constraints.
